  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 230 AM Tuesday... \n\nKEY MESSAGE 1... Seasonable and dry fall weather will persist across \ncentral NC into Thursday. Then much cooler weather again by late \nweek through the weekend, with dryness likely well into next week. \n\nThe combined circulation of surface high pressure over eastern \nCanada and an area of low pressure that will linger off the mid-\nAtlantic coast through mid-week will result in a dry northerly flow \nfor much of the week. Another area of high pressure will build into \neastern Canada and New England toward the weekend reinforcing the \ndry northerly flow across central NC. \n\nThis weather pattern will support a dry forecast through the weekend \nwith temperatures ranging close to average for this time of year \nthrough Thursday. Highs generally 68-74. Low in the mid 40s to \naround 50.\n\nThen, forecast guidance is in close agreement with temperatures \ncooling down with highs in the upper 50s to lower 60s by Saturday. \nThere may be risk of patchy frost by Saturday and Sunday, especially \nnorth and west of the Triangle.",
